:: ---- db.widgets.off (preference) ------------------------------------
::P|db.widgets.off|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.001|COUPER LE FLUX WIDGETS
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.002|
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.003|  Ce que c est    : La strategie Dsh qui commande toute la fonction
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.004|                    Widgets, plus deux boutons de barre des taches par
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.005|                    utilisateur que l'ancien script deplacait avec elle.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.006|
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.007|  Effet reel      : Ecrit AllowNewsAndInterests=0 et TaskbarDa=0. Ne
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.008|                    masque plus le bouton Vue des taches : c'etait un
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.009|                    degat collateral, et tous les profils ecrivent
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.010|                    desormais ShowTaskViewButton=1.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.011|
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.012|  Gain            : C'est l'un des rares gains reellement demontrables de
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.013|                    tout le volet confidentialite : avec la strategie a 0,
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.014|                    l'hote Widgets et son moteur WebView2 ne demarrent
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.015|                    jamais, donc un moteur de navigateur cesse d'etre
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.016|                    resident et cesse de telecharger des actualites a
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.017|                    intervalle regulier. Sur un portable, cela signifie
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.018|                    aussi que la machine ne se reveille plus pour
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.019|                    rafraichir une vignette meteo.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.020|
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.021|  Cout            : Plus de meteo d'un coup d'oeil ni de panneau
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.022|                    d'actualites. WIN+W ne repond plus.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.023|
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.024|  Defaut Windows  : Strategie absente, les deux boutons affiches.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.025|
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.026|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.027|    AllowNewsAndInterests=0 :
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.028|        Coupe la fonction Widgets pour toute la machine. Le panneau ne
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.029|        s'ouvre plus, WIN+W ne fait rien, et l'hote Widgets ainsi que son
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.030|        moteur WebView2 ne sont plus lances : c'est la seule valeur du
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.031|        groupe qui supprime un vrai processus et un vrai trafic reseau
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.032|        periodique.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.033|    AllowNewsAndInterests=1 :
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.034|        Explicitement autorise par strategie. Troisieme etat qui marque le
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.035|        reglage comme gere ; ce n'est pas l'etat d'origine.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.036|    AllowNewsAndInterests=DELETE :
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.037|        Absente, l'etat d'origine. Widgets disponible et commande par le
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.038|        reglage normal de la barre des taches.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.039|    TaskbarDa=0          : Masque le bouton Widgets pour l'utilisateur
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.040|                           courant. Cosmetique en soi : la fonction reste
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.041|                           installee et peut encore tourner. Associez-la a
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.042|                           la strategie ci-dessus si vous voulez supprimer
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.043|                           le processus, pas seulement le bouton.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.044|    TaskbarDa=1          : Bouton affiche, la valeur d'origine habituelle.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.045|    ShowTaskViewButton=0 : Masque le bouton Vue des taches. Purement
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.046|                           visuel : les bureaux virtuels fonctionnent
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.047|                           toujours avec WIN+TAB et pas un octet de
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.048|                           memoire n'est economise. Cela n'a aucun rapport
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.049|                           avec Widgets et n'a ete regroupe ici que par
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.050|                           accident.
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.051|    ShowTaskViewButton=1 : Bouton affiche : la valeur d'origine, et ce
::T|FR|db.widgets.off.052|                           qu'ecrivent desormais tous les profils.
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Commencez par le correctif : la version
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.002|                         precedente masquait le bouton Vue des taches
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.003|                         comme effet de bord de la coupure de Widgets, ce
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.004|                         qui n'economisait rien et privait les gens d'une
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.005|                         commande qu'ils utilisent tous les jours. C'est
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.006|                         repare : aucun profil ne le masque. Sur le flux
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.007|                         lui-meme, gaming, serveur et portable ecrivent 0,
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.008|                         pour la meme raison reelle declinee de trois
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.009|                         facons : un WebView2 resident qui telecharge du
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.010|                         contenu en continu n'a sa place ni a cote d'un
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.011|                         jeu, ni sur une machine dont la bande passante
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.012|                         appartient a Plex, ni sur une batterie. La
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.013|                         bureautique garde Widgets et se confond donc
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.014|                         exactement avec la ligne Windows, parce que ce
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.015|                         profil a pour role de laisser les fonctions
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.016|                         actives et qu'un foyer regarde reellement la
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.017|                         meteo plus souvent qu'il ne remarque la memoire
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.018|                         consommee.
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.019|
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.020|  Problemes connus : Avec AllowNewsAndInterests=0, l'entree Widgets
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.021|                     disparait completement des parametres de la barre des
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.022|                     taches au lieu d'y apparaitre decochee, et WIN+W
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.023|                     reste inerte. Rien d'autre n'en depend.
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.024|
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.025|  Non verifie (en)  : I did not measure the Widgets footprint on 25H2;
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.026|                      quoted figures range from roughly 100 to 300 MB and
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.027|                      depend on whether the board has been opened since
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.028|                      boot, so treat the memory number as an order of
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.029|                      magnitude rather than a measurement. TaskbarDa=1 is
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.030|                      the stock consumer value but OEM and EEA images
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.031|                      vary, so p5 is 'the usual default', not a universal
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.032|                      one.
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.033|
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.034|  Cible           : reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Dsh" /v
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.035|                    "AllowNewsAndInterests" /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f ; reg add
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.036|                    "HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explor
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.037|                    er\Advanced" /v "TaskbarDa" /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f ; reg
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.038|                    add same key /v "ShowTaskViewButton" /t REG_DWORD /d 0
::X|FR|db.widgets.off.039|                    /f (OPTY.bat lines 1724-1726)
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.001|SHUT THE WIDGETS FEED DOWN
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.002|
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.003|  What it is      : The Dsh policy that governs the whole Widgets feature,
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.004|                    plus two per-user taskbar buttons the old script moved
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.005|                    along with it.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.006|
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.007|  Actual effect   : Writes AllowNewsAndInterests=0 and TaskbarDa=0. It no
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.008|                    longer hides the Task View button - that was
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.009|                    collateral damage and every profile now writes
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.010|                    ShowTaskViewButton=1.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.011|
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.012|  Gain            : This is one of the few genuinely substantiable wins in
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.013|                    the privacy set: with the policy at 0 the Widgets host
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.014|                    and its WebView2 renderer are never started, so a
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.015|                    browser engine stops being resident and stops fetching
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.016|                    news on a timer. On a laptop that also means the
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.017|                    machine stops waking to refresh a weather tile.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.018|
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.019|  Cost            : No weather at a glance and no news panel. WIN+W stops
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.020|                    responding.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.021|
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.022|  Windows default : Policy absent, both buttons shown.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.023|
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.024|  Possible values:
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.025|    AllowNewsAndInterests=0 :
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.026|        Turns the Widgets feature off for the whole machine. The board
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.027|        cannot be opened, WIN+W does nothing, and the Widgets host and its
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.028|        WebView2 renderer are no longer spawned - this is the only value
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.029|        in the group that removes a real process and real periodic network
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.030|        traffic.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.031|    AllowNewsAndInterests=1 :
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.032|        Explicitly allowed by policy. A third state that marks the setting
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.033|        managed; not the shipped condition.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.034|    AllowNewsAndInterests=DELETE :
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.035|        Absent, the shipped state. Widgets available and governed by the
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.036|        normal taskbar setting.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.037|    TaskbarDa=0          : Hides the Widgets button for the current user.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.038|                           Cosmetic on its own - the feature stays
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.039|                           installed and can still run. Pair it with the
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.040|                           policy above if you want the process gone, not
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.041|                           just the button.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.042|    TaskbarDa=1          : Button shown, the usual stock value.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.043|    ShowTaskViewButton=0 : Hides the Task View button. Purely visual -
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.044|                           virtual desktops still work with WIN+TAB and
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.045|                           not a single byte of memory is saved. It has no
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.046|                           relationship to Widgets and was bundled here by
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.047|                           accident.
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.048|    ShowTaskViewButton=1 : Button shown - the shipped value, and what
::T|EN|db.widgets.off.049|                           every profile writes now.
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.001|  Why these profiles : Read the change first: the previous version hid the
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.002|                       Task View button as a side effect of killing
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.003|                       Widgets, which saved nothing and cost people a
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.004|                       control they use daily. That is fixed - no profile
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.005|                       hides it. On the feed itself, gaming, server and
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.006|                       laptop all set 0, for the same real reason in three
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.007|                       different accents: a resident WebView2 that
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.008|                       periodically pulls content is unwanted next to a
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.009|                       game, on a box whose bandwidth belongs to Plex, and
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.010|                       on a battery. Office keeps Widgets and so matches
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.011|                       the Windows row exactly, because that profile's job
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.012|                       is to leave features on and a household really does
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.013|                       glance at the weather more often than it notices
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.014|                       the memory.
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.015|
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.016|  Known problems  : With AllowNewsAndInterests=0 the Widgets entry
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.017|                    disappears from taskbar settings entirely rather than
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.018|                    appearing unchecked, and WIN+W is inert. Nothing else
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.019|                    depends on it.
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.020|
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.021|  Unverified      : I did not measure the Widgets footprint on 25H2;
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.022|                    quoted figures range from roughly 100 to 300 MB and
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.023|                    depend on whether the board has been opened since
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.024|                    boot, so treat the memory number as an order of
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.025|                    magnitude rather than a measurement. TaskbarDa=1 is
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.026|                    the stock consumer value but OEM and EEA images vary,
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.027|                    so p5 is 'the usual default', not a universal one.
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.028|
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.029|  Target          : reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Dsh" /v
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.030|                    "AllowNewsAndInterests" /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f ; reg add
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.031|                    "HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explor
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.032|                    er\Advanced" /v "TaskbarDa" /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f ; reg
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.033|                    add same key /v "ShowTaskViewButton" /t REG_DWORD /d 0
::X|EN|db.widgets.off.034|                    /f (OPTY.bat lines 1724-1726)
