:: ---- reg.appcaptureenabled (preference) -----------------------------
::P|reg.appcaptureenabled|0|0|1|1|1|
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.001|CAPTURES GAME BAR DESACTIVEES (APPCAPTUREENABLED = 0)
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.002|
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.003|  Ce que c est    : L'interrupteur par utilisateur des captures d'ecran et
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.004|                    clips de la Game Bar, sous HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Win
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.005|                    dows\CurrentVersion\GameDVR. Il forme une paire avec
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.006|                    GameDVR_Enabled sous HKCU\System\GameConfigStore.
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.007|
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.008|  Effet reel      : Ecrit 0 dans HKCU, volontairement pas sous Policies.
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.009|                    La capture s'arrete mais Parametres > Jeux > Captures
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.010|                    reste utilisable, au lieu d'etre grise sous une
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.011|                    banniere « organisation ».
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.012|
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.013|  Gain            : Rend l'autre moitie de la paire reellement effective :
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.014|                    avec GameDVR_Enabled=0 seul, la Game Bar peut encore
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.015|                    armer la capture. Aucune promesse de FPS ici, et il ne
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.016|                    faut pas en faire : il s'agit de savoir quel outil
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.017|                    possede vos raccourcis d'enregistrement, pas de
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.018|                    performance.
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.019|
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.020|  Cout            : WIN+ALT+ImprEcr et WIN+ALT+R ne produisent plus de
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.021|                    fichiers. Tout le reste de la Game Bar - la surcouche,
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.022|                    le compteur de performances, les widgets - continue de
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.023|                    fonctionner.
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.024|
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.025|  Defaut Windows  : 1 sur toute installation ou la Game Bar a deja tourne.
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.026|
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.027|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.028|    1                    : La capture Game Bar est armee : WIN+ALT+ImprEcr
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.029|                           prend une capture d'ecran, WIN+ALT+R lance un
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.030|                           clip, et si l'enregistrement en arriere-plan
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.031|                           est actif, le pipeline maintient un tampon
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.032|                           glissant. La page Parametres > Jeux > Captures
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.033|                           reste pleinement utilisable.
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.034|    0                    : La capture ne produit plus de fichiers et les
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.035|                           raccourcis ne font rien. Comme la valeur est
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.036|                           ecrite dans HKCU et volontairement PAS sous
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.037|                           Policies, la page Parametres reste modifiable
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.038|                           et aucune banniere « gere par votre
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.039|                           organisation » n'apparait : vous pouvez la
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.040|                           reactiver depuis l'interface. C'est cette
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.041|                           valeur qui rend GameDVR_Enabled=0 reellement
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.042|                           effectif : avec celle-la seule, la Game Bar
::T|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.043|                           peut encore armer la capture.
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Le profil jeu choisit 0 : quiconque a installe
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.002|                         OBS, ShadowPlay ou la surcouche AMD a deja un
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.003|                         enregistreur et ne veut pas que deux outils se
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.004|                         disputent les memes raccourcis. Le serveur
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.005|                         choisit 0 par proprete sur une machine sans
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.006|                         personne au clavier - pas comme un gain, et il ne
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.007|                         faut pas le vendre comme tel. Bureautique et
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.008|                         portable gardent le 1 d'origine, parce que « tout
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.009|                         fonctionne » inclut le raccourci de capture
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.010|                         d'ecran que quelqu'un utilise peut-etre deja, et
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.011|                         que le couper ne leur rapporte rien de mesurable.
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.012|                         Repondez ici comme vous avez repondu pour
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.013|                         GameDVR_Enabled : les deux vont ensemble.
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.014|
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.015|  Non verifie (en)  : Whether AppCaptureEnabled exists on a clean 25H2
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.016|                      image before Game Bar has ever run was not verified;
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.017|                      OPTY writes it either way, which is harmless. No
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.018|                      frame-rate claim is attached to this setting in
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.019|                      either direction - the 'GameDVR costs you FPS' story
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.020|                      concerns background recording actually being active,
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.021|                      not the presence of this value.
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.022|
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.023|  Cible           : HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\GameDVR
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.024|                    /v AppCaptureEnabled /t REG_DWORD (OPTY.bat line 2113
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.025|                    writes 0 in the mapping path; line 1671 writes 1 in
::X|FR|reg.appcaptureenabled.026|                    :gaming_restore)
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.001|GAME BAR CAPTURES OFF (APPCAPTUREENABLED = 0)
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.002|
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.003|  What it is      : The per-user switch for Game Bar screenshots and
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.004|                    clips, under HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVe
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.005|                    rsion\GameDVR. It is one half of a pair with
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.006|                    GameDVR_Enabled under HKCU\System\GameConfigStore.
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.007|
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.008|  Actual effect   : Writes 0 in HKCU, deliberately not under Policies.
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.009|                    Capture stops while Settings > Gaming > Captures stays
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.010|                    usable, instead of being greyed out under an
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.011|                    organisation banner.
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.012|
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.013|  Gain            : It makes the other half of the pair stick - with
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.014|                    GameDVR_Enabled=0 alone, Game Bar can still arm
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.015|                    capture. There is no frame-rate claim here and none
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.016|                    should be made: this is about which tool owns your
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.017|                    recording hotkeys, not about performance.
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.018|
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.019|  Cost            : WIN+ALT+PrtScn and WIN+ALT+R stop producing files.
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.020|                    Everything else in Game Bar - the overlay, the
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.021|                    performance counter, the widgets - keeps working.
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.022|
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.023|  Windows default : 1 on any installation where Game Bar has run.
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.024|
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.025|  Possible values:
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.026|    1                    : Game Bar capture is armed: WIN+ALT+PrtScn takes
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.027|                           a screenshot, WIN+ALT+R starts a clip, and if
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.028|                           Background recording is also on, the capture
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.029|                           pipeline holds a rolling buffer. The Settings >
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.030|                           Gaming > Captures page stays fully usable.
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.031|    0                    : Capture stops producing files and the hotkeys
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.032|                           do nothing. Because this is written in HKCU and
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.033|                           deliberately NOT under Policies, the Settings
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.034|                           page stays editable and no 'managed by your
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.035|                           organisation' banner appears - you can turn it
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.036|                           back on from the GUI. This is the value that
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.037|                           makes GameDVR_Enabled=0 actually stick: with
::T|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.038|                           that one alone, Game Bar can still arm capture.
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.001|  Why these profiles : Gaming picks 0 because anyone who has installed
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.002|                       OBS, ShadowPlay or the AMD overlay already has a
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.003|                       recorder and does not want two of them fighting
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.004|                       over the same hotkeys. Server picks 0 as tidiness
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.005|                       on a box with no one at the keyboard - not as a
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.006|                       gain, and it should not be sold as one. Office and
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.007|                       laptop keep the shipped 1, because 'everything
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.008|                       works' includes the screenshot shortcut somebody
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.009|                       may already be using, and turning it off buys them
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.010|                       nothing measurable. Answer this the same way you
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.011|                       answered GameDVR_Enabled - they are a pair.
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.012|
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.013|  Unverified      : Whether AppCaptureEnabled exists on a clean 25H2 image
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.014|                    before Game Bar has ever run was not verified; OPTY
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.015|                    writes it either way, which is harmless. No frame-rate
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.016|                    claim is attached to this setting in either direction
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.017|                    - the 'GameDVR costs you FPS' story concerns
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.018|                    background recording actually being active, not the
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.019|                    presence of this value.
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.020|
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.021|  Target          : HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\GameDVR
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.022|                    /v AppCaptureEnabled /t REG_DWORD (OPTY.bat line 2113
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.023|                    writes 0 in the mapping path; line 1671 writes 1 in
::X|EN|reg.appcaptureenabled.024|                    :gaming_restore)
