::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.001|STORAGE SENSE SCHEDULE: MONTHLY
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.002|
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.003|  What it is      : How often Storage Sense wakes up on its own. Accepted
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.004|                    values are 0 (only when free space is low), 1 (daily),
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.005|                    7 (weekly) and 30 (monthly). OPTY writes 30.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.006|
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.007|  Actual effect   : Sets StoragePolicy value 2048 to 30. Windows switches
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.008|                    from 'react to a nearly full disk' to 'run once a
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.009|                    month regardless'.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.010|
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.011|  Gain            : Cleanup happens before the disk is in trouble instead
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.012|                    of during the panic. There is no throughput, latency
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.013|                    or FPS benefit and none is claimed - the benefit is
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.014|                    purely that you never meet the low-disk-space warning,
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.015|                    and that installers stop failing for want of a couple
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.016|                    of GB.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.017|
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.018|  Cost            : One short, low-priority cleanup pass per month, at a
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.019|                    moment Windows picks. On a laptop it may briefly spin
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.020|                    the disk. That is the entire cost.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.021|
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.022|  Windows default : 0 - 'During low free disk space'.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.023|
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.024|  Possible values:
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.025|    0                    : 'During low free disk space' - the shipped
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.026|                           value. Storage Sense stays dormant and only
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.027|                           wakes when Windows decides free space is
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.028|                           critical, which in practice means the cleanup
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.029|                           happens at the worst possible moment: while you
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.030|                           are already out of room, often while an install
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.031|                           or an update is failing for that reason.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.032|    1                    : Every day. The pass is short and low priority,
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.033|                           but on a machine that produces little temp
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.034|                           churn it is a daily scan for nothing.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.035|                           Reasonable only on a box that genuinely fills
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.036|                           up in days.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.037|    7                    : Every week. The right choice if you install and
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.038|                           uninstall software constantly, or if the disk
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.039|                           is small enough that a month of accumulation is
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.040|                           visible.
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.041|    30                   : Every month. Cleanup happens on a calendar
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.042|                           instead of in a panic. On a normal machine a
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.043|                           month of temp files is a few hundred MB to a
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.044|                           couple of GB - enough to be worth removing,
::T|EN|storagesense.cadence.045|                           small enough that the pass is quick.
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.001|  Why these profiles : Four identical answers, and the reason is that this
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.002|                       knob has no performance dimension whatsoever, so
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.003|                       gaming, server, office and laptop have nothing to
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.004|                       disagree about - inventing a weekly-for-the-server
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.005|                       split would be a fake distinction, especially since
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.006|                       Storage Sense never touches the downloads or media
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.007|                       a server actually accumulates. The only real split
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.008|                       in the table is 30 versus WINDOWS's 0, which is the
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.009|                       genuine choice: run on a calendar, or wait for the
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.010|                       panic. Pick 7 yourself if you churn software
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.011|                       constantly.
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.012|
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.013|  Target          : HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Storage
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.014|                    Sense\Parameters\StoragePolicy /v "2048" /t REG_DWORD
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.015|                    - OPTY.bat line 892, call :regset "%SSP%" "2048"
::X|EN|storagesense.cadence.016|                    REG_DWORD 30 "run every 30 days"
::
:: ---- storagesense.downloads.off (repair) ------------------------
::P|storagesense.downloads.off|0|0|0|0|0|
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.001|VERROU DE SECURITE : NE JAMAIS VIDER TELECHARGEMENTS
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.002|
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.003|  Ce que c est    : L'Assistant Stockage possede une regle separee capable
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.004|                    de supprimer les fichiers de votre dossier
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.005|                    Telechargements passe un certain age. Elle est
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.006|                    desactivee par defaut, mais un ancien outil
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.007|                    d'optimisation ou un clic curieux a pu l'armer. Cette
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.008|                    etape force ses deux moities sur OFF.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.009|
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.010|  Effet reel      : Ecrit les valeurs StoragePolicy 32=0 et 512=0, soit «
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.011|                    ne pas nettoyer Telechargements » et « seuil d'age :
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.012|                    jamais ». Ce sont les valeurs d'origine : sur une
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.013|                    machine intacte c'est une reaffirmation, sur une
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.014|                    machine ou l'une des deux etait armee c'est une vraie
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.015|                    reparation.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.016|
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.017|  Gain            : Ca garantit qu'activer l'Assistant Stockage a l'etape
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.018|                    precedente ne peut pas heriter d'une regle
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.019|                    Telechargements deja armee. Sans ce verrou, OPTY
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.020|                    serait la cause de la disparition de vos
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.021|                    telechargements un mois plus tard - c'est exactement
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.022|                    l'incident que cette fiche existe pour empecher.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.023|
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.024|  Cout            : Rien. C'est une pure mesure de securite, et c'est de
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.025|                    toute facon la valeur par defaut de Windows. Vous
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.026|                    pouvez toujours activer vous-meme le nettoyage des
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.027|                    Telechargements dans Parametres > Systeme > Stockage >
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.028|                    Assistant Stockage si vous y tenez.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.029|
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.030|  Defaut Windows  : 32=0 et 512=0 - la suppression automatique des
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.031|                    Telechargements est desactivee, seuil d'age « Jamais
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.032|                    ». Ecrire 0 ici, c'est la valeur livree, pas une
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.033|                    troisieme position.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.034|
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.035|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.036|    32=0                 : Regle de nettoyage des Telechargements
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.037|                           desactivee. L'Assistant Stockage ne regarde
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.038|                           jamais dans %USERPROFILE%\Telechargements.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.039|                           C'est la valeur d'origine et celle qu'OPTY
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.040|                           ecrit pour tous les profils.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.041|    32=1                 : Regle de nettoyage des Telechargements armee. A
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.042|                           chaque passage planifie, les fichiers du
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.043|                           dossier Telechargements qui n'ont pas ete
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.044|                           ouverts depuis plus longtemps que le seuil de
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.045|                           la valeur 512 sont supprimes definitivement -
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.046|                           pas envoyes a la Corbeille. C'est le reglage
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.047|                           qui devore les installateurs, les factures et
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.048|                           les torrents que les gens gardaient exprès.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.049|    512=0                : Seuil d'age « Jamais ». Associe a 32=0, c'est
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.050|                           ceinture et bretelles : meme si quelque chose
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.051|                           remet 32 a 1 plus tard, un seuil « Jamais »
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.052|                           signifie qu'aucun fichier n'est assez vieux
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.053|                           pour etre eligible.
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.054|    512=1 / 14 / 30 / 60 : Seuil d'age en jours. Toute valeur non nulle
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.055|                           ici est une munition chargee des l'instant ou
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.056|                           la valeur 32 passe a 1 : 512=1 signifie qu'un
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.057|                           fichier telecharge hier et jamais rouvert
::T|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.058|                           disparait au passage suivant.
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq reponses identiques, et c'est toute la
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.002|                         raison d'etre de la fiche : c'est un garde-fou,
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.003|                         pas une preference. Il n'existe aucun role de
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.004|                         machine - jeu, hebergement, bureautique, mobilite
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.005|                         - pour lequel la suppression definitive et
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.006|                         automatique du dossier Telechargements soit le
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.007|                         bon comportement, et WINDOWS est d'accord puisque
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.008|                         0 est la valeur livree. Une distinction entre
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.009|                         profils voudrait dire qu'un des cinq arme
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.010|                         deliberément une regle de perte de donnees, ce
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.011|                         qu'aucun ne devrait faire.
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.012|
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.013|  Cible           : HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Storage
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.014|                    Sense\Parameters\StoragePolicy /v "32" /t REG_DWORD
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.015|                    and /v "512" /t REG_DWORD - OPTY.bat lines 897-898,
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.016|                    call :regset "%SSP%" "32" REG_DWORD 0 and call :regset
::X|FR|storagesense.downloads.off.017|                    "%SSP%" "512" REG_DWORD 0
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.001|SAFETY PIN: NEVER AUTO-DELETE DOWNLOADS
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.002|
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.003|  What it is      : Storage Sense has a separate rule that can delete
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.004|                    files in your Downloads folder once they reach a
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.005|                    chosen age. It is off by default, but a previous
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.006|                    tweaking tool or a curious click can have armed it.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.007|                    This step forces both halves of it off.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.008|
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.009|  Actual effect   : Writes StoragePolicy values 32=0 and 512=0 - 'do not
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.010|                    clean Downloads' and 'age threshold: never'. Both are
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.011|                    the shipped values, so on an untouched machine this is
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.012|                    a re-assert; on a machine where either was armed it is
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.013|                    a genuine repair.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.014|
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.015|  Gain            : It guarantees that turning Storage Sense on in the
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.016|                    step above cannot inherit an already-armed Downloads
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.017|                    rule. Without this pin, OPTY would be the thing that
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.018|                    started deleting your downloads a month later - which
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.019|                    is the concrete failure this whole card exists to
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.020|                    prevent.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.021|
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.022|  Cost            : Nothing. This is a pure safety measure and it is the
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.023|                    Windows default anyway. You can still turn Downloads
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.024|                    cleanup on yourself in Settings > System > Storage >
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.025|                    Storage Sense if you actually want it.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.026|
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.027|  Windows default : 32=0 and 512=0 - Downloads auto-delete is off, age
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.028|                    threshold 'Never'. Writing 0 here is the shipped
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.029|                    value, not a third state.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.030|
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.031|  Possible values:
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.032|    32=0                 : Downloads cleanup rule off. Storage Sense never
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.033|                           looks inside %USERPROFILE%\Downloads. This is
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.034|                           the shipped value and the one OPTY writes for
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.035|                           every profile.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.036|    32=1                 : Downloads cleanup rule armed. During each
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.037|                           scheduled pass, files in the Downloads folder
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.038|                           that have not been opened for longer than the
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.039|                           threshold in value 512 are deleted permanently
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.040|                           - not moved to the Recycle Bin. This is the
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.041|                           setting that eats installers, invoices and
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.042|                           torrents people were keeping on purpose.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.043|    512=0                : Age threshold 'Never'. Paired with 32=0 it is
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.044|                           belt and braces: even if something later flips
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.045|                           32 to 1, a threshold of Never means no file is
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.046|                           old enough to qualify.
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.047|    512=1 / 14 / 30 / 60 : Age threshold in days. Anything non-zero here
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.048|                           is live ammunition the moment value 32 becomes
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.049|                           1: 512=1 means a file you downloaded yesterday
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.050|                           and have not reopened is deleted on the next
::T|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.051|                           pass.
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.001|  Why these profiles : Five identical answers, and that is the entire
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.002|                       point of the card: this is a guard rail, not a
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.003|                       preference. There is no machine role - gaming,
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.004|                       hosting, office, portable - for which unattended
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.005|                       permanent deletion of the Downloads folder is the
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.006|                       right behaviour, and WINDOWS agrees because 0 is
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.007|                       what Windows ships. A profile split here would mean
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.008|                       one of the five profiles deliberately arming a
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.009|                       data-loss rule, which none of them should.
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.010|
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.011|  Target          : HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Storage
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.012|                    Sense\Parameters\StoragePolicy /v "32" /t REG_DWORD
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.013|                    and /v "512" /t REG_DWORD - OPTY.bat lines 897-898,
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.014|                    call :regset "%SSP%" "32" REG_DWORD 0 and call :regset
::X|EN|storagesense.downloads.off.015|                    "%SSP%" "512" REG_DWORD 0
::
:: ---- office.c2r.update (preference) ---------------------------------
::P|office.c2r.update|SKIP|SKIP|RUN|RUN|SKIP|
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.001|FORCER UNE MISE A JOUR MICROSOFT 365 / OFFICE
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.002|
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.003|  Ce que c est    : Office installe via Microsoft 365 utilise le moteur
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.004|                    Click-to-Run, qui se met a jour selon le calendrier de
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.005|                    son canal. Cette etape lance OfficeC2RClient.exe
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.006|                    /update user pour qu'il verifie et installe
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.007|                    immediatement.
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.008|
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.009|  Effet reel      : Demarre une mise a jour interactive. Office peut
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.010|                    demander de fermer Word, Excel ou Outlook pour
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.011|                    terminer. Rien n'est configure : le canal et le
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.012|                    calendrier restent inchanges.
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.013|
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.014|  Gain            : Vous recuperez tout de suite les correctifs de
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.015|                    securite et de bogues au lieu d'attendre votre tour
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.016|                    dans le canal. Les documents Office font partie des
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.017|                    deux ou trois vecteurs de logiciels malveillants les
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.018|                    plus utilises : une version d'Office perimee est une
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.019|                    exposition reelle, pas un detail cosmetique. Sur une
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.020|                    machine restee hors ligne ou inutilisee des mois, le
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.021|                    rattrapage peut etre important.
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.022|
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.023|  Cout            : Du temps et de la bande passante, et il faudra peut-
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.024|                    etre fermer des applications Office en plein travail.
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.025|                    Une fois installee, une version d'Office ne se retire
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.026|                    qu'a la main avec officec2rclient.exe /update user
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.027|                    updatetoversion=<version>, et encore faut-il connaitre
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.028|                    le numero de version voulu.
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.029|
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.030|  Defaut Windows  : Sans objet - Office se met a jour tout seul selon son
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.031|                    canal ; ceci ne fait que forcer l'operation
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.032|                    maintenant, ce qui n'est l'etat d'origine de rien.
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.033|
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.034|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.035|    RUN                  : Lance OfficeC2RClient.exe /update user. Click-
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.036|                           to-Run contacte le CDN Office, compare la
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.037|                           version installee a la tete de votre canal de
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.038|                           mise a jour, puis telecharge et applique le
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.039|                           differentiel. L'argument « user » rend
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.040|                           l'operation interactive : une fenetre de
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.041|                           progression apparait et Office peut demander de
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.042|                           fermer Word, Excel ou Outlook pour terminer. Ni
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.043|                           le canal ni le calendrier ne sont modifies.
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.044|    SKIP                 : Rien n'est lance. Click-to-Run continue de se
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.045|                           mettre a jour au rythme de son canal - le canal
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.046|                           actuel environ une fois par mois, le canal
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.047|                           Entreprise mensuel le deuxieme mardi, le canal
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.048|                           semestriel deux fois par an. Refuser, c'est
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.049|                           attendre son tour, pas rester sans correctifs
::T|FR|office.c2r.update.050|                           indefiniment.
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Le vrai axe ici n'est pas la performance mais «
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.002|                         Office est-il installe et y a-t-il quelqu'un
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.003|                         devant l'ecran ». BUREAUTIQUE et PORTABLE
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.004|                         l'executent : ce sont les deux machines qui ont
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.005|                         reellement Word, Excel et Outlook, elles sont
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.006|                         surveillees, et un Office perime est un trou de
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.007|                         securite, pas une lenteur. Branchez le portable
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.008|                         au secteur d'abord : une mise a jour de canal
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.009|                         complete, c'est quelques centaines de Mo et du
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.010|                         CPU soutenu, exactement ce que le profil «
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.011|                         batterie d'abord » n'aime pas. SERVEUR refuse
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.012|                         parce que la commande est interactive et qu'une
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.013|                         machine sans ecran n'a personne pour repondre a «
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.014|                         fermez Outlook pour continuer », et parce
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.015|                         qu'Office y est rarement installe. GAMING refuse
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.016|                         pour une question de moment, pas de principe.
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.017|                         WINDOWS refuse parce que forcer une mise a jour
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.018|                         maintenant n'est pas le comportement d'origine.
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.019|
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.020|  Problemes connus : Il n'y a aucun garde « if exist » sur le chemin. Sur
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.021|                     toute machine sans Office Click-to-Run - pas d'Office
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.022|                     du tout, ou une installation MSI perpetuelle - la
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.023|                     ligne s'execute quand meme et CMD affiche « Le chemin
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.024|                     d'acces specifie est introuvable. » dans la console,
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.025|                     pendant que le journal d'OPTY note tout de meme «
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.026|                     Launched OfficeC2RClient.exe /update user ». L'etape
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.027|                     reste ensuite bloquee sur un pause, en attente d'une
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.028|                     touche que l'utilisateur ne sait pas justifier. Par
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.029|                     ailleurs, si Outlook tourne avec un .ost ouvert, la
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.030|                     mise a jour patiente jusqu'a sa fermeture, et la
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.031|                     fenetre peut finir derriere la console d'OPTY, ou
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.032|                     elle passe facilement inapercue.
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.033|
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.034|  Cible           : OPTY.bat :office_update, line 1405: "C:\Program
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.035|                    Files\Common Files\microsoft
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.036|                    shared\ClickToRun\OfficeC2RClient.exe" /update user -
::X|FR|office.c2r.update.037|                    called with no if exist guard
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.001|FORCE A MICROSOFT 365 / OFFICE UPDATE
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.002|
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.003|  What it is      : Office installed from Microsoft 365 uses the Click-to-
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.004|                    Run engine, which updates itself on its own channel
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.005|                    schedule. This step launches OfficeC2RClient.exe
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.006|                    /update user to make it check and install right now.
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.007|
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.008|  Actual effect   : Starts an interactive update. Office may ask you to
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.009|                    close Word, Excel or Outlook to finish. Nothing is
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.010|                    configured - the update channel and schedule are
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.011|                    unchanged.
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.012|
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.013|  Gain            : You get security fixes and bug fixes immediately
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.014|                    instead of whenever the channel gets round to you.
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.015|                    Office documents are one of the two or three most-used
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.016|                    malware delivery routes, so a stale Office build is a
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.017|                    real exposure and not a cosmetic one. On a machine
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.018|                    that has been offline or unused for months this can be
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.019|                    a large catch-up.
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.020|
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.021|  Cost            : Time and bandwidth, and you may have to close Office
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.022|                    applications mid-work. Once installed, an Office build
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.023|                    can only be rolled back manually with
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.024|                    officec2rclient.exe /update user
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.025|                    updatetoversion=<build>, and you need to know the
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.026|                    build number you want.
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.027|
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.028|  Windows default : Not applicable - Office updates automatically on its
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.029|                    channel schedule; this only forces it now, which is
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.030|                    not a shipped state.
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.031|
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.032|  Possible values:
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.033|    RUN                  : Launches OfficeC2RClient.exe /update user.
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.034|                           Click-to-Run contacts the Office CDN, compares
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.035|                           the installed build against the head of your
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.036|                           update channel, and downloads and applies the
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.037|                           delta. The 'user' argument makes it
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.038|                           interactive: a progress window appears and
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.039|                           Office may ask you to close Word, Excel or
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.040|                           Outlook before it can finish. Nothing about the
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.041|                           channel or the schedule is changed.
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.042|    SKIP                 : Nothing is launched. Click-to-Run keeps
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.043|                           updating on its own channel cadence - Current
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.044|                           Channel ships roughly monthly, Monthly
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.045|                           Enterprise on the second Tuesday, Semi-Annual
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.046|                           twice a year. Skipping means waiting your turn,
::T|EN|office.c2r.update.047|                           not going unpatched forever.
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.001|  Why these profiles : The honest axis here is not performance but 'is
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.002|                       Office installed and is somebody sitting in front
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.003|                       of it'. OFFICE and LAPTOP run it: those are the two
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.004|                       machines that actually have Word, Excel and Outlook
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.005|                       on them, they are attended, and an out-of-date
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.006|                       Office is a genuine security hole rather than a
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.007|                       slow one. Plug the laptop in first - a full channel
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.008|                       update is a few hundred MB and sustained CPU, which
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.009|                       is the one thing the battery-first profile
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.010|                       dislikes. SERVER skips because the command is
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.011|                       interactive and a headless box has nobody to answer
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.012|                       'close Outlook to continue', and because Office is
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.013|                       rarely installed there at all. GAMING skips on
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.014|                       timing, not principle. WINDOWS skips because
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.015|                       forcing an update now is not the shipped behaviour.
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.016|
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.017|  Known problems  : There is no 'if exist' guard on the path. On any
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.018|                    machine without Click-to-Run Office - no Office at
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.019|                    all, or a perpetual MSI installation - the line runs
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.020|                    anyway and CMD prints 'The system cannot find the path
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.021|                    specified.' into the console, while OPTY's log still
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.022|                    records 'Launched OfficeC2RClient.exe /update user'.
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.023|                    The step then sits on a pause waiting for a keypress
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.024|                    that the user has no context for. Separately, if
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.025|                    Outlook is running with an open .ost the update stalls
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.026|                    until Outlook is closed, and the window can end up
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.027|                    behind OPTY's console where it is easy to miss.
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.028|
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.029|  Target          : OPTY.bat :office_update, line 1405: "C:\Program
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.030|                    Files\Common Files\microsoft
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.031|                    shared\ClickToRun\OfficeC2RClient.exe" /update user -
::X|EN|office.c2r.update.032|                    called with no if exist guard
::
