:: ---- dt.mpo.off (risky) ----------------------------------------
::P|dt.mpo.off|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|DELETE|
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.001|DESACTIVER LE MPO (CONTOURNEMENT ANTI-SCINTILLEMENT)
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.002|
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.003|  Ce que c est    : L'interrupteur de dernier recours contre le
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.004|                    scintillement et les flashs noirs en multi-ecran : il
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.005|                    force chaque fenetre a passer par le compositeur au
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.006|                    lieu de laisser le controleur d'affichage la sortir
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.007|                    depuis son propre plan materiel.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.008|
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.009|  Effet reel      : Ecrit OverlayTestMode=5, OverlayMinFPS=0 et
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.010|                    DisableOverlays=1. Redemarrage necessaire.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.011|
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.012|  Gain            : Parfois, sur certaines versions de pilote, cela stoppe
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.013|                    les flashs noirs ou le scintillement d'un montage
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.014|                    multi-ecran a frequences differentes. Souvent, non -
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.015|                    et rien dans le registre ne dit si le MPO est bien
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.016|                    votre cause : le seul test consiste a l'ecrire,
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.017|                    redemarrer, observer. Ce n'est en aucun cas un reglage
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.018|                    de performance : cela retire un chemin materiel
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.019|                    rapide, cela n'en ajoute pas. Quiconque presente cela
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.020|                    comme un reglage FPS le prend a l'envers.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.021|
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.022|  Cout            : Chaque image en fenetre repasse par une composition
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.023|                    complete de DWM : plus de consommation GPU et un etage
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.024|                    de latence en plus en fenetre et en borderless. Le VRR
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.025|                    cesse de fonctionner en borderless, et les fonctions
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.026|                    bâties sur ce chemin de presentation - mode fenetre
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.027|                    optimise, Auto HDR pour les jeux en fenetre - sont
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.028|                    largement signalees comme partant avec.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.029|
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.030|  Defaut Windows  : Les trois absentes, MPO actif.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.031|
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.032|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.033|    SKIP                 : Laisse les trois valeurs exactement en l'etat.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.034|                           Sur une machine normale elles sont deja
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.035|                           absentes et il ne se passe rien ; sur une
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.036|                           machine ou quelqu'un a applique ce
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.037|                           contournement, SKIP le laisse en place - et
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.038|                           c'est voulu, parce que la personne qui l'a
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.039|                           applique en a peut-etre encore besoin.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.040|    DELETE               : Supprime les trois, ce qui est le vrai defaut
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.041|                           Windows. Pas 0 : l'absence. Ecrire des zeros
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.042|                           laisserait un forcage ecrit valant zero, un
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.043|                           troisieme etat que ni Windows ni le
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.044|                           contournement ne produisent jamais.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.045|    OverlayTestMode=5 (+ OverlayMinFPS=0, DisableOverlays=1) :
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.046|        Le contournement lui-meme. DWM cesse de proposer des plans
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.047|        materiels au pilote : chaque image en fenetre est fondue dans le
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.048|        bitmap du bureau par le compositeur avant d'atteindre la dalle.
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.049|        Des trois, seule OverlayTestMode=5 est la valeur reellement
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.050|        publiee par Microsoft et les fabricants de GPU ; les deux autres
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.051|        viennent de scripts copies-colles et leur effet n'est pas
::T|FR|dt.mpo.off.052|        documente. Redemarrage necessaire.
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre SKIP et un DELETE : c'est la forme honnete
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.002|                         pour un contournement guide par un symptome, et
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.003|                         non pour une preference. Aucun profil ne le
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.004|                         choisit : il n'existe pas de type de machine qui
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.005|                         se porte mieux avec le chemin materiel coupe,
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.006|                         seulement une machine precise avec un
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.007|                         scintillement precis sur un pilote precis. Donc 1
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.008|                         a 4 n'y touchent pas, et 5 supprime les valeurs,
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.009|                         parce que le defaut Windows est ici l'absence et
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.010|                         non zero. Si vous en voulez, choisissez-le a la
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.011|                         main dans le menu affichage, apres avoir deja
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.012|                         essaye un autre cable, du DisplayPort plutot que
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.013|                         du HDMI, une reinstallation propre du pilote et
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.014|                         l'alignement des frequences de rafraichissement :
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.015|                         cela regle le probleme plus souvent que le
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.016|                         registre.
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.017|
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.018|  Problemes connus : C'est l'application du reglage qui casse quelque
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.019|                     chose, et c'est concret : les jeux en fenetre sans
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.020|                     bordure perdent le taux de rafraichissement variable
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.021|                     et restent a la frequence du bureau. L'utilisateur
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.022|                     accuse alors l'ecran ou le cable. Si le VRR ne
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.023|                     fonctionne plus en borderless sur une machine «
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.024|                     optimisee » par quelqu'un d'autre, c'est la premiere
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.025|                     valeur a chercher.
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.026|
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.027|  Non verifie (en)  : The exact feature list lost when MPO is disabled
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.028|                      varies by driver, and the Auto HDR and Optimized
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.029|                      Windowed Mode dependencies are widely reported
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.030|                      rather than verified here. The VRR-in-borderless
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.031|                      loss is the one I would state without hedging. Also:
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.032|                      only OverlayTestMode=5 is a published value;
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.033|                      OverlayMinFPS and DisableOverlays are carried along
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.034|                      by convention and OPTY writes them because removal
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.035|                      scripts expect all three, not because their effect
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.036|                      is known.
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.037|
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.038|  Cible           : reg add HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\Dwm /v
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.039|                    OverlayTestMode REG_DWORD 5 ; same key /v
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.040|                    OverlayMinFPS REG_DWORD 0 ; reg add
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.041|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.042|                    /v DisableOverlays REG_DWORD 1 - OPTY.bat label
::X|FR|dt.mpo.off.043|                    :dt_mpo_off, lines 2062-2064
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.001|DISABLE MULTI-PLANE OVERLAY (FLICKER WORKAROUND)
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.002|
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.003|  What it is      : The last-resort switch for multi-monitor flicker and
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.004|                    black flashing: it forces every window through the
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.005|                    compositor instead of letting the display controller
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.006|                    scan a window out of its own hardware plane.
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.007|
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.008|  Actual effect   : Writes OverlayTestMode=5, OverlayMinFPS=0 and
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.009|                    DisableOverlays=1. Reboot required.
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.010|
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.011|  Gain            : Sometimes, on some driver versions, it stops black
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.012|                    flashes or flicker on a multi-monitor setup with
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.013|                    mismatched refresh rates. Often it does not, and there
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.014|                    is no way to tell from the registry whether MPO is
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.015|                    your cause - the only test is set it, reboot, watch.
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.016|                    It is not a performance tweak in any sense: it removes
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.017|                    a hardware fast path, it does not add one. Anyone
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.018|                    presenting this as an FPS setting has it backwards.
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.019|
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.020|  Cost            : Every windowed frame goes back through a full DWM
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.021|                    composite pass, so higher GPU power draw and one more
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.022|                    stage of latency in windowed and borderless play. VRR
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.023|                    in borderless stops working, and the presentation-path
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.024|                    features layered on top - Optimized Windowed Mode,
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.025|                    Auto HDR for windowed games - are widely reported to
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.026|                    go with it.
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.027|
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.028|  Windows default : All three absent, MPO on.
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.029|
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.030|  Possible values:
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.031|    SKIP                 : Leaves the three values exactly as they are. On
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.032|                           a normal machine they are already absent and
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.033|                           nothing happens; on a machine where somebody
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.034|                           applied this workaround, SKIP keeps it applied
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.035|                           - which is the point, because the person who
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.036|                           applied it may still need it.
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.037|    DELETE               : Removes all three, which is the actual Windows
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.038|                           default. Not 0 - absence. Writing zeros here
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.039|                           would leave a written override that reads as
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.040|                           zero, which is a third state neither Windows
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.041|                           nor the workaround ever produces.
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.042|    OverlayTestMode=5 (+ OverlayMinFPS=0, DisableOverlays=1) :
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.043|        The workaround itself. DWM stops offering hardware planes to the
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.044|        driver, so every windowed frame is blended into the desktop bitmap
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.045|        by the compositor before it reaches the panel. Of the three, only
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.046|        OverlayTestMode=5 is the value Microsoft and the GPU vendors
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.047|        actually published; the other two ride along from copy-pasted
::T|EN|dt.mpo.off.048|        scripts and their effect is undocumented. Reboot required.
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.001|  Why these profiles : Four skips and one delete, which is the honest
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.002|                       shape for a symptom-driven workaround rather than a
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.003|                       preference. No profile picks this: there is no kind
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.004|                       of machine that is better off with the hardware
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.005|                       path switched off, only a specific machine with a
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.006|                       specific flicker on a specific driver. So 1 to 4
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.007|                       leave it alone, and 5 deletes the values, because
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.008|                       the Windows default here is absence and not zero.
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.009|                       If you want it, choose it by hand from the display
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.010|                       menu after you have already tried a different
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.011|                       cable, DisplayPort instead of HDMI, a clean driver
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.012|                       install, and matching the refresh rates - those fix
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.013|                       this more often than the registry does.
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.014|
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.015|  Known problems  : Applying it is what causes the breakage, and it is
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.016|                    concrete: borderless windowed games lose variable
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.017|                    refresh rate and sit at the desktop refresh rate.
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.018|                    Users then blame the monitor or the cable. If VRR
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.019|                    stopped working in borderless on a machine that has
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.020|                    been optimised by someone else, this is the first
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.021|                    value to look for.
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.022|
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.023|  Unverified      : The exact feature list lost when MPO is disabled
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.024|                    varies by driver, and the Auto HDR and Optimized
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.025|                    Windowed Mode dependencies are widely reported rather
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.026|                    than verified here. The VRR-in-borderless loss is the
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.027|                    one I would state without hedging. Also: only
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.028|                    OverlayTestMode=5 is a published value; OverlayMinFPS
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.029|                    and DisableOverlays are carried along by convention
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.030|                    and OPTY writes them because removal scripts expect
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.031|                    all three, not because their effect is known.
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.032|
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.033|  Target          : reg add HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\Dwm /v
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.034|                    OverlayTestMode REG_DWORD 5 ; same key /v
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.035|                    OverlayMinFPS REG_DWORD 0 ; reg add
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.036|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.037|                    /v DisableOverlays REG_DWORD 1 - OPTY.bat label
::X|EN|dt.mpo.off.038|                    :dt_mpo_off, lines 2062-2064
